Q: Fetching related details from the model in a loop only returns that last iteration&#39;s data in CodeIgniter A: <p>This is an XY Problem. You shouldn't need to iterate over query results, nor make multiple trips to your model. Use a <code>join()</code> in your query builder script so that the member details are appended to the incident data.</p>
<p>Model:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getIncidentsWithMembers(): array
{
    return $this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select('i.id,m.f_name,m.m_name,m.l_name')
        -&gt;join('member m', 'i.member_id = m.id')
        -&gt;get('incident i')
        -&gt;result_array();
}
</code></pre>
<p>Controller:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function index()
{
    $data['incidents'] = $this-&gt;incident_model-&gt;getIncidentsWithMembers();
    $this-&gt;load-&gt;view('incident_list', $data);
}
</code></pre>
<p>View:</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>foreach ($incidents as $row) {
    printf('%d: %s %s %s', $row['id'], $row['f_name'], $row['m_name'], $row['l_name']);
}
</code></pre>
